.TH PATINA-LOCK 1 "2026-10-19" "patina-desktop 0.1.0" "Patina Desktop"
.SH NAME
patina-lock \- lock screen of the Patina desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B patina-lock
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B patina-lock
locks the session and shows the sign-in screen for the signed-in user on every display: the
time and date, the user, and a password field. The session unlocks when the right password is
typed. Passwords are checked with PAM, service
.BR patina-lock .
.PP
The compositor starts it on Ctrl+Alt+L, before the computer sleeps, after 15 minutes without
input, and when asked with
.BR "loginctl lock-session" .
If it stops while the session is locked, the screen stays black and locked; Ctrl+Alt+L starts
it again.
.PP
The button bottom-left shows the other users; picking one asks LightDM to show that user's
sign-in (with other display managers it is dimmed). The button bottom-right shuts the
computer down.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/patina-lock
PAM configuration for checking the password.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR patina-compositor (1),
.BR patina-greeter (1)
